items.core_explanation_md:
Pick a random starting point within the first interval, then take every k-th item after it. To audit every twentieth voucher in a register, start at a random voucher among the first twenty and continue in steps of twenty.

Three things to remember:

- every item has an equal chance of selection, **but not every possible sample does**: items next to each other can never be picked together;
- it is quick and often cheaper than simple random sampling;
- it can mislead when the interval lines up with a **pattern** in the list. Sampling every seventh day of cash withdrawals could pick only pay-days, for example.
